---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Audience Research &amp; Targeting | Kelp Agency"
  description="Identify the buyers, questions, and decision points that should shape your messaging, campaigns, and website experience."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Digital Marketing Services"
    title="Audience Targeting"
    description="Marketing gets expensive fast when you are talking to everyone. We identify the audiences most likely to care, convert, and justify the spend behind your campaigns."
    lottieFile="audience-targeting.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of marketing underperforms because the audience is too broad. The
        message tries to reach everyone, the spend gets scattered, and the
        people seeing the campaign are not the people most likely to act.
      </p>
      <p>
        That makes every other decision harder, from creative direction to
        channel choice to budget allocation.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We look at the business, the offer, the existing data, and the behavior
        of the people you need to reach. From there we define clearer segments,
        identify what matters to each one, and shape targeting around real
        intent instead of guesses.
      </p>
      <h2>Replace Assumptions with Useful Evidence</h2>
      <p>
        We review customer and sales input, campaign results, search intent,
        site behavior, and the differences between high-value customer groups.
        Then we define practical segments: the problem, trigger, objections,
        proof needed, and likely next step. Those segments guide creative and
        page content; they are not personas written to sit in a slide deck.
      </p>
      <h2>Put the Insight to Work</h2>
      <p>
        Audience findings can shape campaign targeting, service-page structure,
        product navigation, and follow-up. We measure whether the resulting
        enquiries or sales fit the business, not simply whether a broader
        audience clicks. Work with Kelp on a clearer marketing plan.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        A useful audience is defined by its problem and context, not only age or
        job title. We look at what different buyers need to understand, who
        influences the decision, and where those people seek information. The
        output can inform landing pages, offers, ad groups, creative, and
        follow-up messages. When the evidence is thin, we make the assumptions
        visible and learn from actual enquiries.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Audience and buying-situation research</li>
        <li>Message priorities by segment</li>
        <li>Landing-page and campaign recommendations</li>
        <li>A measurement plan for lead or order quality</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        We begin with the customers you most want more of and the enquiries that
        currently waste your team's time. That contrast helps us target the
        right problem before refining channels.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Do we need new personas?</h3>
      <p>
        Only if they help decisions. A short, evidence-based description of the
        buying situation is often more useful than a long fictional profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Clarify Your Audience
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={77} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
